// `o?.f ?? d` where `f` is a NESTED-STRUCT field. `vl check` returns 0 and the emitter refuses
// with `emitProgram: `?.` over a nullable struct has no `if` blocktype for this field's rep`.
// Should print 11 then 12.
//
// MECHANISM. The `?.`…`??` arm spells its `if` blocktype through `fbIfForSharedField`, which is
// keyed on the field CODE alone; a code-15 (nested-struct) result needs the field's own TARGET
// ROW to spell `(ref $S)`, so `optChainFieldCodeOk` declines it. The site already knows that row
// (`nsi` / `nfi`), which is what makes this look one-line.
//
// IT IS NOT ONE LINE, AND THE NULLABLE FIELD IS WHY. A code-15 slot is nullable STORAGE whether
// the field is declared `S` or `S | null`. For a declared `S` the else arm may `ref.as_non_null`;
// for `S | null` it may not, because `o?.f ?? d` must yield `d` when the FIELD is null too, and
// an unconditional recovery would TRAP rather than coalesce. The fix must read the declaration,
// not the code.
//
// EVERY OTHER DELIVERY POSITION FOR THIS VALUE RUNS (D1084): equality both ways, annotated and
// inferred bindings, return, argument, local and global assignment, struct-field, list element,
// and a two-hop chain. This is the one position that did not close with them, and it is a
// separate, older site.
type S = { a: i32 }
type T = { f: S }

function firstA(o: T | null, d: S) { return (o?.f ?? d).a }

const s: S = { a: 11 }
const d: S = { a: 12 }
const t: T = { f: s }

print(firstA(t, d))
print(firstA(null, d))
